<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Georg Forster</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1754–1794</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Georg Forster was a German naturalist and writer who sailed with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-cook">James Cook</a> on his second voyage and wrote a famous account of it. As librarian at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mainz">Mainz</a> he joined the Jacobin club and helped lead the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhenish-german-national-convention">Rhenish-German National Convention</a> of the Republic of Mainz in 1793. He went to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> to seek union with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and died there.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/georg-forster.jpg" alt="Georg Forster" width="320" height="407" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Johann Heinrich Wilhelm Tischbein · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Georg_Forster.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
